# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` (Dockerfile:12) sends the entire working tree to
# the Docker daemon. Measured before this file existed:
#
#     .env            present   ← a developer's real credentials
#     .git/           15 MB
#     node_modules/   240 MB
#     total context   ~268 MB
#
# `.gitignore` does not help here. `.gitignore` and `.dockerignore` are
# independent files, and Docker reads only the latter — so gitignoring `.env`
# does nothing for `docker build`.
#
# The published image was verified NOT to contain `.env` (the runtime stage
# copies only `dist/`), so this is not a secret-in-the-shipped-artefact problem.
# It is that the context is uploaded, and that `COPY . .` writes these paths into
# a builder layer that persists in the build cache — readable by anyone with
# access to the builder or the cache.
#
# Verified with a canary: with this file absent, a planted `.env`,
# `.git/` and `node_modules/` were all present in the build context.

# Dependencies — installed inside the image, and huge.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Secrets and local configuration. The single most important entry here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets/
!src/db/migrations/

# Version control and CI
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Build output — rebuilt inside the image, and `dist` can be large
dist
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm
.cache

# Local scratch
*.log
*.tmp
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# Agent and planning material — not part of the product
plan.md
tasks/
docs/
!docs/SECURITY.md

# Documentation is not needed to run the server
*.md
!README.md
!SECURITY.md
!LICENSE

# Tests — not shipped, and they carry test-only credentials.
#
# `packages/*/src` is deliberately NOT excluded: the builder stage runs
# `npm run build:sdk`, which compiles packages/keystone-sdk/src. Excluding it was
# tried and the image stopped building — a .dockerignore that breaks the build is
# worse than a large context.
src/tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.js
frontend/src
frontend/e2e
